<Base title="About & Academic Background" description="Andrea Rausa is a postdoctoral researcher and SU2 developer at Politecnico di Milano, with a Ph.D. in Aerospace Engineering." section="about">
  <div class="page-hero"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Background</p><h1>About Andrea.</h1><p>Postdoctoral researcher in aerospace engineering, with a focus on CFD methods, scientific software development, and reproducible numerical evidence.</p></div></div>
  <section class="section"><div class="container split">
    <div class="prose"><p class="section-label">Profile</p><h2>From physical modelling to reliable computation.</h2><p>I am a postdoctoral researcher in the Department of Aerospace Science and Technology at Politecnico di Milano. I obtained my Ph.D. in Aerospace Engineering in 2024, following my bachelor's and master's degrees at the same institution.</p><p>My research covers computational aerodynamics, unsteady and separated flows, icing, RANS modelling, numerical verification, and scalable CFD workflows. Alongside research publications, I contribute directly to the development of the open-source SU2 solver.</p><p>In teaching roles, I have supported courses in computational fluid dynamics, fluid dynamics, and aerodynamics.</p><div class="buttons"><a class="button outline" href="mailto:andrea.rausa@polimi.it?subject=CV%20request">Request current CV ↗</a><a class="button outline" href="https://aero.polimi.it/it/personale/andrea.rausa" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Institutional profile ↗</a></div><p style="font-size:12px">A new PDF CV will be linked after final content review; the outdated website PDF is not presented as current.</p></div>
    <div><p class="section-label">Education & appointments</p><div class="timeline">
      <div class="timeline-entry"><small>2024 – present</small><h3>Postdoctoral Researcher</h3><p>Politecnico di Milano · Department of Aerospace Science and Technology</p></div>
      <div class="timeline-entry"><small>2020 – 2024</small><h3>Ph.D. in Aerospace Engineering</h3><p>Politecnico di Milano</p></div>
      <div class="timeline-entry"><small>2017 – 2020</small><h3>M.Sc. in Aeronautical Engineering</h3><p>Politecnico di Milano · 110/110 cum laude</p></div>
      <div class="timeline-entry"><small>2014 – 2017</small><h3>B.Sc. in Aerospace Engineering</h3><p>Politecnico di Milano</p></div>
    </div></div>
  </section>
